---@field conflictDetailLevel? aws.codecommit.ConflictDetailLevelTypeEnum|string The level of conflict detail to use. If unspecified, the default FILE_LEVEL is used, which returns a not-mergeable result if the same file has differences in both branches. If LINE_LEVEL is specified, a conflict is considered not mergeable if the same file in both branches has differences on the same line.
---@field conflictResolutionStrategy? aws.codecommit.ConflictResolutionStrategyTypeEnum|string Specifies which branch to use when resolving conflicts, or whether to attempt automatically merging two versions of a file. The default is NONE, which requires any conflicts to be resolved manually before the merge operation is successful.
---@field commitMessage? aws.codecommit.Message The commit message to include in the commit information for the merge.
---@field authorName? aws.codecommit.Name The name of the author who created the commit. This information is used as both the author and committer for the commit.
---@field email? aws.codecommit.Email The email address of the person merging the branches. This information is used in the commit information for the merge.
---@field keepEmptyFolders? aws.codecommit.KeepEmptyFolders If the commit contains deletions, whether to keep a folder or folder structure if the changes leave the folders empty. If true, a .gitkeep file is created for empty folders. The default is false.
---@field conflictResolution? aws.codecommit.ConflictResolution If AUTOMERGE is the conflict resolution strategy, a list of inputs to use when resolving conflicts during a merge.

